WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:02.180
My name is Taiki Kudou.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.190
I wound up in the Digital World,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.880
where I met Shoutmon 
and the other Digimon.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.430
This world is having a lot of trouble

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.320
<b>Team Bagra</b>

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.320
<b>Team Twilight      Xros Heart (Team Taiki)   Team Blue Flare</b>

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.320
Protagonist                                                                  Rival

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.140
with the attacking Bagra Army.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.930
We came to the Dust Zone,

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:17.400
where we saved our new ally, 
Nene, from the hands of evil.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.970
Then we got our seventh Code Crown.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:29.970
<b>Wisemon</b>

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:29.970
<b>and the Secrets of the Digital World!</b>

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.750
Wisemon and the Secrets 
of the Digital World!

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.880
Come on, let's go to the next Zone.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:40.550
What's wrong?

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:42.230
Do you feel sick?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.280
No. I'm fine.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.890
Really? You look sort of pale...

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:53.670
Taiki Kudou! You don't understand 
a woman's heart at all!

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.230
Huh? And you do?

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.500
Of course!

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.640
Just look at that 
adorable, restless pose.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.970
Nene is being bashful...

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:06.320
About becoming our... no, <i>my</i> companion!

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.620
That's obviously just your own delusion.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:10.780
Definitely a delusion. 
Never gonna happen.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.680
Your own delusion.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:14.720
It is not a delusion!

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.760
<i>DarkKnightmon, where is my brother?</i>

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.150
<i>Where is Yuu?</i>

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:22.990
<i>Give Yuu back to me!</i>

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:26.500
<i>Nene, I have no further use for you.</i>

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.100
I have to find Yuu.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.140
Change Zone!

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.140
What's wrong, Nene?

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.470
I can't use my Xros Loader...

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.020
Nene?!

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.420
Hey, what happened?!

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:51.020
Nene!

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.890
She really was sick, 
just like Taiki said!

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.790
Nene!

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.630
It's likely that being held 
captive by DarkKnightmon

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.670
caused so much fatigue that 
she reached her breaking point.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:06.070
What?! Hey, Televimon...

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.480
That's Monitamon!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.790
Can't you do something?!

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.980
I know!

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.770
If we go to the Monitamons' 
home village,

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:20.920
we can restore Miss Nene's health!

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.100
Really?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:23.290
Then let's go there right away!

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.990
But we can't use Miss 
Nene's Xros Loader.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.360
Sparrowmon and you Monitamons 
can get in my Xros Loader.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.360
Oh, good idea!

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.360
Okay, let's go!

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:43.340
Change Zone!

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.510
Are we close to the exit yet?

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.920
You should see it soon.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.090
What is that?

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:02.840
Why is there a Digimon here?

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.200
Th-That's...

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.800
Arkadimon!

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:09.390
It's a legendary Digimon 
that makes its nest

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.780
in the Digital space between Zones,

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.370
where it traps all who pass 
through and eats them.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.030
Th—

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:15.790
That's...

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:16.510
Run!

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.520
Guys!

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.230
Are you going to eat me?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.600
Certainly not.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:42.800
I can't put you out of 
your misery that easily...

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.470
my little red General.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.370
Lilithmon!

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.340
Now then, what shall I do with you?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.210
After what you put me 
through in the Dust Zone,

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.920
I feel like I could just explode.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.820
I'll torment you...

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.480
to distract myself from my rage!

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:06.620
The Xros Loader is mine.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:10.600
All your friends, human 
and Digimon alike,

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.360
have fallen prey to Arkadimon.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:18.040
You will drift about the space 
between the Zones for eternity

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.220
as you envision how your 
friends will meet their end!

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.460
What a lovely feeling!

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.760
Now, Arkadimon, it's dinnertime.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.590
You may eat everything 
except the Xros Loader.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.230
Ow!

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.140
That hurt...

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.360
Huh? What is this book?

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.340
Very interesting.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.690
Specimen has awakened at Digi-time 4077.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.960
He looks around with 
a vacant expression.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.330
He has noticed me, and looks suspicious.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.630
What is this? Where am I?

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.690
"What is this? Where am I?"

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:21.340
These are the specimen's first words.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.300
Wait a minute... Specimen?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.250
Do you mean m—

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.070
Ow...

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:29.740
What is this?!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.480
Hmm, a human?

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.650
And he was not atomized 
in the Digital realm...

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.120
A truly interesting creature.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.140
Right, then...

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.390
Let us begin the dissection.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.660
No! Stop!

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:02.190
He's hungry?

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:04.350
Let's see...

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.470
Hey, he's got DigiNoir!

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:12.750
I was so immersed in my research,

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.580
I forgot to eat.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:19.010
Though you are but a specimen, 
I owe you my life.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.360
I cannot dissect you now.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.420
You sure are strange.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:25.660
I'm Taiki Kudou. Who are you?

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.870
I am Wisemon, a seeker of wisdom.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.450
I spend my days in this book, 
conducting research

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:35.690
to solve the mysteries 
of the Digital World.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.880
Book? You mean...

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.740
This research lab exists within my book,

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.230
which drifts about the Digital realm.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.150
This book is protected 
by a unique power,

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.350
so it cannot be atomized and disappear.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:54.070
The data of travelers between 
Zones flows through this realm,

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:56.290
telling me various things 
about the outside world.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.980
It is ideal for my research.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.570
Wow...

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.820
Still, I thought you

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:07.210
would be worth researching, 
simply because you're a human,

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:10.040
but to think you would be the 
General I've heard about...

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:13.170
Where is the device that makes 
it possible to DigiXros?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:14.380
And the Code Crowns?

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:18.050
My Xros Loader was sent 
somewhere by a Digimon

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:20.730
called Arkadimon, along with my friends.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.240
I have seven Code Crowns,

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.770
but they're all inside the Xros Loader.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.190
Oh...

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:27.690
Hey, Wisemon...

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.430
Will you help me?

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.980
I have to save my friends, quickly.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.070
One of them is sick.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:36.870
It's best to give up.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.680
Arkadimon is one nasty Digimon.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:42.340
If the Bagra Army has 
him on their side...

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.630
They're already done for.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.840
What's that?

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:59.290
Huh? Knightmon?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.690
What are you guys doing?

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:09.000
Th-Th-That's the Digimon from before!

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.500
You two woke up at the 
worst possible moment.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:17.340
What is that thing? It's so scary!

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:19.680
Is it... hungry?

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.510
We're inside Arkadimon's nest.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.850
Knightmon and the PawnChessmons

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.630
are protecting us with a barrier of light.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:34.780
Darn it! I can't take this anymore!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.560
PawnChessmon, open an exit for me!

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.960
Rock Dama—

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.460
What are you doing?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.470
You won't last five minutes out there!

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:58.250
Taiki! Where did you go?!

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:24.790
So this is what the great 
Lord Bagramon looks like.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.740
So silent, yet such an 
intimidating presence!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:31.280
My heart is pounding. 
This must be love...

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:34.740
And? How do the records stand?

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:39.850
Sir! There are a total of 108 
Code Crowns among all the Zones.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:43.630
Of those, I possess 26,

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:45.890
Blastmon has 22,

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:49.830
and Lilithmon has acquired 24.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:54.500
Also, the blue team, Blue Flare, has 11.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:59.670
The team known as Twilight seems 
to have no interest in Code Crowns.

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:01.930
And the red team?

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:05.040
Xros Heart possesses seven Code Crowns.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.750
Eighteen Zones are yet to be invaded.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:11.050
Xros Heart is already done for.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:11.580
What?!

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:17.140
Once I get their Code 
Crowns, I'll have 31.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:18.720
That puts me at the top of 
the Three Head Officers.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:21.070
Splendid, Lilithmon.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:24.130
You may be the one fit 
to be my successor.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:25.420
What?!

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.270
I am honored, Lord Bagramon!

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:28.920
What?!

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.600
I wish to see it as 
quickly as possible...

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.240
The moment when we acquire 
all the Code Crowns,

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:40.810
and the new, evil Digital World 
is reconstructed by my hand!

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:47.220
If he obtains all 108 
of the Code Crowns,

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.450
the entire Digital World...

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.620
will be at the mercy of Bagramon.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:58.030
Without a doubt, our world 
would become a living hell.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.370
A living hell...

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:05.240
I'm sure it would influence 
your own human world, as well.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:07.760
I get it! So that's why that happened!

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:18.550
Was the Digital World born of digital 
technology created by humans?

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.910
The other way around.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:25.970
The Digital World existed 
long before the human world.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:33.050
You humans only recently learned 
how to use a part of our world.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:39.910
The digital zone used by 
humans amounts to, perhaps...

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:41.990
this much of the total.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:44.000
That's all?

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:47.820
B-But if a world this big

00:12:47.820 --> 00:12:50.420
turns into the evil world 
that the Bagra Army wants...

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:51.970
That would be awful...

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:54.150
What's so bad about that?

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:57.700
If it means I'll get to see the 
Digital World be reborn,

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.940
it doesn't matter to me whether 
the result is good or bad.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:02.230
I am interested only in whether

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:05.500
the inferences derived from 
my research are correct.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:07.710
Now...

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:11.390
I will not dissect you, 
but I will continue my research.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:16.570
I will now resume my study of 
your body, my little specimen.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.300
Stop it!

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:25.620
<i>Those are...</i>

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:35.050
We're in trouble if this keeps up!

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:39.020
What can we do without Taiki?

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:42.490
I have a great idea.

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:46.640
Let's use these DigiMemories 
I brought from the castle.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:50.000
You had all these? 
Why didn't you say so sooner?!

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.950
I didn't get a chance to.

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:53.930
I told you...

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.110
Taiki isn't here!

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:57.970
And Nene's still unconscious.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:00.330
Who's supposed to use the DigiMemories?

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.470
I don't like those looks...

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.160
No way I'm going out there!

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.390
What? What did you say?

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.330
Please! You have to let me go outside!

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.940
If you go out there, 
Arkadimon will eat you.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.770
This is the only safe place.

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:18.270
I'm not kidding!

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.800
My friends might get eaten!

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.010
I can't turn my back on my friends!

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:24.860
Can't turn your back...

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.520
I don't understand this phenomenon.

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:28.990
Wisemon,

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:32.500
you've never seen a Zone with 
your own eyes, have you?

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:33.330
No.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.450
Since the Digital World was divided, 
I have always remained here.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.710
If you saw all the Digimon 
out there who are suffering,

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.190
your body would act before 
you can even think about it.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:45.090
That is the "can't turn 
your back" phenomenon?

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.330
But no matter what you do, it's useless.

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:49.840
My long years of research tell me that

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:52.700
the Bagra Army is going to win. 
That is the conclusion.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:57.070
I'm... no, we, in Xros Heart,

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:59.180
are going to change that conclusion!

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.210
What?

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.190
Wisemon, please!

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:03.880
Let me out of here!

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:08.890
Do as you please. I'm busy.

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.920
I have no time to bother with you.

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:16.140
Lend us your strength...

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:17.300
<b>Darkdramon</b>

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:17.300
<b>Attack: Gigastick 
Lance</b>

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.300
Darkdramon!

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:18.460
DigiMemory!

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:22.780
It's no use...

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.290
Now it's do or die!

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.710
We'll go out there and 
fight it ourselves!

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:32.350
Hey!

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:33.260
Is that...

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.110
It can't be!

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:35.150
Hey!

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:37.930
It's Taiki! Taiki's here!

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.850
But how did he get here?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.690
Hey, guys!

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:44.910
Sorry I took so long!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:46.860
I'll be right there, okay?!

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.380
He swam through the Digital realm?

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.150
Just as reckless as ever!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:57.300
Taiki!

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.400
Iron ball kick!

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:02.650
Wow...

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.610
I see! So that's why he had 
an iron ball on his foot!

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:06.390
No!

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:16.490
Taiki!

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:25.280
That book...

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:30.700
Wisemon!

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:45.680
Wisemon...

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.590
You destroyed your 
precious book to save me?

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.260
Its worth is trivial compared to you.

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.550
You are remarkable!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:58.290
It's just like you said... 
my body acted automatically!

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:02.230
This is the "can't turn 
your back" phenomenon!

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:03.570
Wisemon...

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:08.110
I need you to remain alive for 
my future research, as well.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.250
Taiki Kudou!

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:16.860
Take this!

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.350
All right!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.690
Sorry you had to wait, everyone!

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:22.750
Here goes!

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:36.600
Shoutmon!

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:37.740
Okay!

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:38.640
Ballistamon!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.610
Dorulumon!

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.470
Starmons!

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.020
Yes!

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:46.510
Sparrowmon!

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:48.100
DigiXros!

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.050
DigiXros!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.000
Shoutmon X5!

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:19.220
X5, let's save Akari and the others

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.450
and get out of here!

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:22.450
Yeah, no need to hang 
around here any longer!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.280
Knightmon, we're outta here!

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:25.520
Understood!

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.330
PawnChessmon, let us inside!

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:38.530
We're entering the Digital realm!

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:43.030
All right! To the next Zone!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:49.240
You want to eat us that bad?

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:51.040
What's this?

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:53.170
This is...

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:55.480
It's a DigiMemory I 
borrowed from Bastemon!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:59.580
All right, if you want to 
eat something, eat this!

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:01.240
DigiMemory!

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:07.160
Gigastick Lance, activate!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.500
Darkdramon!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.740
Still hungry?

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:22.810
Then eat some of this!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.710
Meteor Impact!

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:36.390
Now we're really going to the next Zone!

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:37.880
Yeah!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:45.050
Arkadimon, where are you?

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.500
I'm...

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:56.530
...going to explode!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.890
Yes! We made it out!

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.820
Thanks, Wisemon!

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:11.320
Huh?

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:13.610
He's gone...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.670
I'm in here, Taiki.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:18.950
Oh, you're in the Xros Loader?

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:21.130
Ah, you have Code Crowns in here!

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:24.080
This will be a fine 
place for my research.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.370
I've decided to continue my 
studies here for a while.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.010
Huh?

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:33.050
And I still intend to study you 
as my experimental specimen.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.160
I'm counting on your cooperation.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.180
Experimental specimen?

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:40.500
That's right! We have to get Nene to...

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:42.720
Enemies?

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:46.160
Are those friends of Monitamon?

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:49.600
So you have made it...

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.500
to the Shinobi Zone.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:58.210
<b>Digimon Data Collection</b>

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:58.210
Digimon Data Collection!

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.150
Listen to the melody of 
this Digimon I caught!

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:00.150
<b>Melody starts in 3 seconds.</b>

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.150
<b>Melody starts in 2 seconds.</b>

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:02.150
<b>Melody starts in 1 second.</b>

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:14.570
<b>[Type]</b>

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:14.570
<b>Flame Type</b>

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:14.570
<b>[Attack]</b>

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:14.550
<b>Ice Phantom 
Cold Flame</b>

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:14.550
Are you hot or cold? Make up your mind!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.890
We're in the Monitamons' 
home, the Shinobi Zone!

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.330
A ninja village full of monitors!

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.110
All we have to do to get the Code Crown

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.900
is make Karatenmon laugh!

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:25.500
This Zone is crazy!

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:27.070
Digimon Xros Wars!

00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:29.430
You can't turn your back 
on the next one, either!

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:29.380
<b>Shinobi Zone,</b>

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.380
<b>the Comic Ninja Battle!</b>
